stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> DRAFT: created by the worker, or by HR on their behalf
    DRAFT --> [*]: abandoned before submission
    DRAFT --> PENDING: submitted, no BLOCK in V1 to V12, HOLD posted
    PENDING --> PENDING: a level approves, further levels remain
    PENDING --> APPROVED: final level approves, AVAIL rows posted per day
    PENDING --> REJECTED: any level rejects with a recorded reason
    PENDING --> WITHDRAWN: worker withdraws before the first leave day
    PENDING --> ESCALATED: leave_timeout_hours elapses, no auto-decision
    ESCALATED --> APPROVED: decided at the escalation level
    ESCALATED --> REJECTED: decided at the escalation level
    ESCALATED --> UNDECIDED_AT_DAY: the first leave day begins undecided
    UNDECIDED_AT_DAY --> APPROVED: decided late, elapsed days re-derive
    UNDECIDED_AT_DAY --> REJECTED: decided late, the absence stands
    APPROVED --> CANCELLED: every day still in the future
    APPROVED --> PART_CANCELLED: some days elapsed, future days reverse
    APPROVED --> CONSUMED: the last leave day passes
    PART_CANCELLED --> CONSUMED: the remaining days pass
    CONSUMED --> RETRO_AMENDED: retro diff for a locked day
    REJECTED --> [*]
    WITHDRAWN --> [*]
    CANCELLED --> [*]
    CONSUMED --> [*]
    RETRO_AMENDED --> [*]
    note right of UNDECIDED_AT_DAY
        Lock gating. The engine never auto
        approves and never auto rejects.
        A queue delay must not become an LOP day.
    end note
    note right of PENDING
        A HOLD reduces available only.
        Balance as at any past date is
        unaffected by approval latency.
    end note
